          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "طماطم (ṭamāṭim) is a modern loan from a European name of the tomato, such as Spanish tomate, which goes back to Nahuatl tomatl. It has no Arabic root."
            }
          ]
        },
